full_description:
Gulbenes municipality is looking for 5 volunteers to work with kids aged from 2 till 7 years old in rural kindergardens in Gulbene county ( Latvia). 
Duties and tasks will be to organise different activities for kids, also daily support for teachers. Work with local community in villades and work with local public institutions - cultural centers, schools etc..

- Accommodation will be in Gulbene town;
- Appartments with all stuff needed for living;
- Pocket money according to  ESC guide, cattering allowance EUR 210;
- Payment for local  transport.

Participant must be ready to work with kids, an explorer, supportive and flexible, full of ideas for activities together with kids, ready to learn and accept

Have you ever wondered how it is to be a scientist? Do you wish to discover life in a unique international institute? Are you motivated by the protection of nature and a wish to experience a new culture in an exciting and friendly environment?  We are currently looking to host  1 European volunteer for 6 or now! The volunteer will work during all the year on differents projects, depending of the needs of the differents teams and on the feeling of the volunteer. He/she will take part of data collecting, field observations (with ornithologists, botanists or ichtyologists…)n  take part of data analysis (on computer) under the responsibility of a project leader. If interest, he/she could work with communication team. For example, your  focus could be mainly (but not only) on the Eurasian Spoonbill research, a beautiful bird with a distinct spoon shape like bill or working with the "Water" team to study river, marshes and sea connections.
More details on https://tourduvalat.org/en/

You will have a room on the site of Tour du Valat, where you will enjoy a communal life with other volunteers and students, with all facilities included (e.g. oven, fridge, heating, internet…) and a fully epuipped kitchen, shard with other residents . During the week you can have lunch in the onsite canteen, where you will try the most delicious French dishes in a familiar environment. You will be allowed to use a car on weekends and for purchase of food in Arles. We take in charge your (green) travel from your country to France, and give you monthly pocket money and extra food allowance.

•	French classes provided by a local teacher if you need language support;
•	Field work best practices like initiation to bird ringing;
•	Database management and data process;
•	Tools for professional life
•	Intercultural exchanges and discover of French life

•	Strong interest for nature conservation; 
•	Curious and adventuress; 
•	Dynamic and resilient;

Youth work, non-formal education – this is what we do. Want to experience life in Latvia while engaging in important local initiatives? Join us for a volunteering experience in the towns of Skrunda and Kuldiga youth houses! We support young people in developing their ideas, participating in local processes, and taking an active role in society. We work with youth councils, run a local Youth Center, support youth initiatives, and organise non-formal educational events such as debates, meetings, and workshops.

As a volunteer, you will join our daily work, support events, and have the chance to share your culture and ideas through activities. There will also be opportunities to develop initiatives with an environmental or sustainability focus, inspiring young people to explore new perspectives on nature and climate change. If you want to spend time learning, contributing, and being part of a team, apply! We are waiting for you!

The volunteer will share an apartment with their private room or live alone in one room apartment, depending on the availability and the circumstances.

During the project you will take part in training course organized by the National Agency where you will meet volunteers from all over Latvia.

Outgoing person from 18 to 30;
Motivated and willing to work with youth and children;
Open for new experiences and personal development;
Able to communicate in English;
Ready to live in a small town in a peaceful, rural and
quiet environment.

Volunteers will take an active role in all activities of Sosyal Fabrika listed below. Sosyal Fabrika offers volunteers: 
Individual and team volunteering; 
International environment; 
Volunteering in youth, health, education and sports fields; 
Personal and professional development; 
Development of soft skills; 
Strong and wide international network; 
A strong relationship with local authorities;
Set of skills in organization management, networking, entrepreneurship, creativity and creative technology, leadership, communication advertising, project management, budget management, activism, etc.

Hosting organization provides accommodation to a volunteer. Volunteers stay in a house. They stay in shared rooms with 2.
All the necessary stuff for beds and rooms will be provided by the hosting organization.
The office is within walking distance, and for further activity places hosting organization covers public transportation expenses.
 Volunteers get a payment as food money in addition to pocket money monthly.

On arrival training.

We are looking for young people between the ages of 18 and 30 who would like to make a difference in the life of other young people and you like to learn more about other cultures. The participants should be willing to share their learnings with young people with fewer opportunities,  to give them a better perspective of their  future on different levels. We are looking for sociable young people, with leadership skills, responsibility, initiative, good capacity for teamwork, organized and empathize with others, communicating skills in English and willing to learn Turkish.

Are you looking for an opportunity to volunteer through the European Solidarity Corps? Join us in Snagov, Romania, and become part of a dedicated team working to create positive change in the local community.

As part of this project, volunteers will: 

- Organise and implement non-formal activities at the A4ACTION Afterschool program such as: outdoor activities, English lessons, arts & crafts, personal development etc.;

- Organize and implement workshops and activities in local schools in Snagov commune, such as: cultural events, civic involvement workshops, green practices and environmental education, digital skills development etc. 

- Create promotional videos to promote the ESC program and the project

- Contribute to the development of the A4ACTION Online Youth Center

Transport cost reimbursement (to come to Romania and to go back to their countries of residence) according to the band distance and the ESC guideline; Pocket and food money according to the ESC guidelines; Accommodation shared with the other volunteers;  Medical insurance during the full volunteering period assured by Henner Insurance Plan.

The volunteers will participate in short workshops and training sessions covering various topics, such as non-formal education, working with kids, facilitation, etc., to support the effective execution of their activities. All activities will employ non-formal education methods. Additionally, volunteers will participate in On Arrival Training and Mid Term Evaluation hosted by the National Agency in Romania.

Age: 18 - 30 years
To have finished secondary school or equivalent finished;
To be unemployed at the time of selection;
Responsible person;
Communicative, friendly and with a positive attitude; 
Interested in the topic of the project; 
Able to prepare and lead an activity; 
Contribute to the development of the A4ACTION Youth Centre;
National of any EU state; 
Good knowledge of English; 
Motivated persons, who're ready to be involved in the local community.

A long term volunteering placement at "Centre de Réadaptation de Mulhouse" (CRM). 

CRM is the biggest Centre in France specialised in health and vocational rehabilitation of adults with physical health problems. It has 3 main activities : Medical care, Vocational training, Social and Cultural activities. 
With the help of the staff members and the local volunteers, the ESC volunteers will perform their tasks within the "Social and Cultural Life" department. They will be assigned the following tasks: 

- To organise workshops for the practice of the English language using non-formal education methods;

- To organise games, film sessions followed by debates and any other activities that would promote the practice of the English language; 

- To take part in the excursions and other leisure outings; 

- A time to learn the French language and work on personal project will be included in volunteers' weekly schedule; 

- Personal initiatives will be encouraged.

Accommodation: The volunteers will be hosted in individual rooms with private bathroom situated in the CRM.
Three meals per day are provided by the Centre's restaurant. Additional food money will be provided too when the volunteer travel and for a few meals outside each month. Monthly city public transportation card will be provided.

Young men and women aged between 22 and 30. They must be friendly, caring and with a certain ease in communication. 

TO APPLY, PLEASE SEND YOUR CV AND COVER LETTER TO >>> OCini@arfp.asso.fr

The project aims to promote sustainable development supporting green, circular and social entrepreneurship for innovation, growth and employment, targeting especially young people and women. It is being implemented in 4 regions of Senegal (Saint-Louis, Louga, Thiès and Dakar) for a period of 3 years in partnership with other NGOs, CSO and local authorities. It is in line with SDG 8 of the 2030 Agenda and it is cofinanced by the Italian Agency for Development Cooperation.
The volunteer will be directly involved supporting local colleagues in:
-	facilitating events organisation (workshops, seminars, trade fairs, meetings, etc.);
-	participating in monitoring project activities;
-	data collection;
-	coordination meetings;
-	communication and awareness-raising activities;
-	narrative and financial reporting

LVIA will provide accommodation at the compound located in the city of Thies (about 300.000 inhabitants), 70 km from Dakar, the capital. In the compound, there are an office and single cottages with separate rooms and private bathrooms, equipped with basic furniture. There is a shared kitchen and dining room. The compound is guarded day and night by wardens. In case of field trips, the organisation will provide transport.

The volunteer will receive Wolof language lessons to be able to relate to community beneficiaries. He/she will also receive a proper presentation of the project, in order to have the possibility to be updated on activities implementation. The Program coordinator will share the basic for project management and administration, to enable the volunteer to play a crucial role in activities implementation. Training on project proposal and writing will be also offered in case any financial opportunity will happen.

LVIA is looking for a person who would like to test himself/herself in a different experience, environment and culture. A person speaking French and willing to travel and move around the territory even with few comforts and who has a spirit of adaptation, preferably with other experiences abroad. A person who knows Office Package very well, who is confident with social media (video and photographic material collection, as well as with capacities to relate on his/her own experiences). Preferably a person with knowledge in economy, agronomy and/or marketing.

Within this project, the volunteer works closely with the Coordination Socio-Culturelle Sainte-Marguerite (CSCSM) and NGO La Baraka, two organisations working in a multicultural setting, in the primary immigration neighbourhood in Liège, Sainte Marguerite. The project is aimed at fighting against marginalisation and social exclusion through the support to disadvantaged youth.

Their work will be primarily focused on:
•	Supporting the in-person courses of French as a Foreign Language for non-francophone teenagers;
•	Implementing common activities with the local associations;
•	Running workshops and discussion groups on various topics, either within the French courses at La Baraka or in collaboration with other member associations;
•	Editing the information bimonthly newspaper «Salut Maurice!»

The volunteers' apartment features two bedrooms and a spacious shared living area. Volunteers will either have a private room or share with another young person, with shared kitchen, bathroom, and toilet facilities. The apartment is equipped with tactile markers on appliances, contrasting tableware, and labelled storage boxes to ensure ease of use and accessibility.

Located in the vibrant Sainte-Marguerite neighbourhood of Liège, the area offers opportunities for independence, supported by mobility and orientation classes.

During their first two weeks, visually impaired volunteers will receive orientation training, as well as sessions on daily living and professional skills. The schedule for these sessions will be arranged in agreement with supervisors, taking into consideration individual needs and preferences. Intensive French classes will also be provided during this period, using adapted materials and taught by a specialised instructor with extensive experience teaching visually impaired students.

We are seeking visually impaired individuals aged between 18 and 30 with a beginner level of French (A2). If you are motivated, eager to be actually involved in the working team, and strive for autonomy in your daily life, you are a perfect fit for this ESC project. Essential qualities include openness, good listening skills, and a genuine desire to make a positive impact.

Venti di Scambio is an association of social promotion  founded in 2009 thanks to a call from the Puglia Region "Principi attivi". The objectives are:
- promote active citizenship of young people;
- promote solidarity, tolerance and understanding between different cultures;
- create a network both at a local level (schools, associations, administrations) and at an international level;
- give young people the opportunity to have a space where they can develop new skills and participate more in community life;
- create an increasingly large number of young people interested in European issues;
- raise young people's awareness of respect for the environment;
- increase youth employment and consequently local development and progress.
We have 1 more spot free and we are searching for a creative person who is ready to get out of comfort zone, developing some "crazy" art, manual but also online stuff with us!
https://mtv2019.wordpress.com/projects/venti-di-scambio-conversano/

The two volunteers hosted in the same moment will live in the city of Conversano. The space is shared by the 2 person. The flat is near to the hosting organization. The apartment is self-managed by the persons who life inside (cleaning, shopping, cooking) and everyone needs to follow basic rule. No party, no guests, personal care of the hosting space.
Every volunteer hosted within ESC program receives on a monthly basis pocket money (5€ per day, about 150 euro) and food money (200 euro). There is no need to use transportation, everything will be in walking distance.

The activities that the volunteers will carry out are, in short
- promoting the NGO activities at schools (middle and high schools) and on the territory, about innovational workshops and EU projects ;
- support in daily life activity of CAOS LAB: collect plastic cups at schools and associations to transform them; 
- support in workshops of 3D design and 3D printing.
- documentation of the activities and update the association’s website, social channels; 
- participate in the training regarding digital competences and development of personal and professionals skills;
- personal project

We search for a person who is very social and wants to interact with various types of people, creative and some art skills, interested in supporting the staff in their main activities linked with innovation (3D design and 3D printing); sustainable development, supporting the staff in the activity of recycling and transformation of plastic; supporting the staff during the workshops in the schools and on the territory; high flexibility; aged 20-30, with a good knowledge of English and minimum basic level of Italian; interested in field of digital tools, art and creativity.

Infopack: https://tinyurl.com/nicmip2026

General Tasks:
-Support the work carried out with local youth, specifically in prospecting the needs of local youth;
-Planning and implementation of inclusive programs aimed at the general community;
-Plan, organize, prepare, implement and evaluate local activities in the field of inclusion, diversity and
equality, support for the Center's trainers and technicians;
-Explore potential international partnerships in the areas of action of Núcleo;
-Develop a project idea and/or a set of activities to implement during the mobility;
-Support in the planning and development of a toolkit of inclusive activities and workshops;
-Support the creation of communication material related to the activities;
-Support in writing reports and templates related to tasks and projects

Summary: 
Accommodation to be defined together with the chosen person.
Food Allowance: daily support according to law + coffee breaks provided at the office
Transport: Financed transport between residence and host location (round trip)
Local transport will be carried out in an ecological way (using public transport or bicycle).
Pocket Money: €180 per month/pax

For more details please contact:
international@nucleodeinclusao.pt

Please read carefully the information provided on the portal: https://youth.europa.eu/solidarity/young-people/training-support_en
In addition to the training stipulated by the CES project, the Inclusion Nucleus provides ongoing training in:
DEI
Communication
Journalism
Project management
Social inclusion
Media Literacy

-Young people aged between 18 and 30 years old;
-Highly motivated to participate in volunteer activities;
-Aware of European values;
-Ability to work in a team;
- With communication capacity;
-Dynamic, participatory, proactive and with a sense of responsibility;
-With a sense of initiative;
-Committed;
-With potential to influence the community;
-No previous experience in volunteering activities promoted by CES.
We will always give preference to young people with fewer opportunities.

Here, at the non-profit kindergarten "Zilvitis" we have developed a unique educational model. We respect and value the individual differences of every child and strive to provide equal opportunities for every child to develop their unique personality. "Zilvitis" is open to all children, who have different interests and abilities and come from a variety of socioeconomic, religious, cultural, and ethnic backgrounds. At our kindergarten, the main activities are educational games, STEAM activities, drama, and learning through experience. TASKS FOR INTERNATIONAL VOLUNTEERS: Help teachers organize various educational activities for children from 1.5 to 7 years old. Take part in organizing STEAM preschool education for children; Organize educational games for children and play with them; Organize various educational activities for children in other EU languages; Organize IT education for preschoolers; Help in the creation of educational spaces and the generation of creative ideas.

- You will receive a private room in a shared flat with other international volunteers, 
- A public transport card, 
- Monthly food and pocket money (~250 euros).

*If needed, we can provide support and provide food products. 

*PLEASE SUBMIT YOUR CV AND MOTIVATIONAL LETTER IN ENGLISH*

- Volunteering group meetings once a month;
- Meeting with a mentor once a month; 
- On-arrival and mid-term training;
- Online language learning;
- Participating in public solidarity events;
- Organization of info/promo solidarity events.

You are an open-minded, patient, motivated individual, willing to work with young children. You can take on new challenges and are eager to learn new things. You are willing to motivate the young and guide them on their educational journey.

The project aims to promote solidarity between generations by involving young volunteers in actions to support elderly people in situations of social isolation. Through activities focused on companionship, well-being and community participation, volunteers contribute to active ageing, the strengthening of social ties and inclusion. The project also provides young people with a non-formal learning experience, developing personal, social and civic skills recognised by Youthpass. It focuses on three main areas: social challenges, health and wellbeing, and education and training.

The host organisation will provide shared accommodation in fully equipped flats that meet Erasmus+ comfort and safety standards. Adequate food will be provided, either through a monthly allowance or meals on site. Local transport costs related to project activities will be covered, ensuring mobility and accessibility throughout the volunteering period.

Volunteers will participate in initial and ongoing training sessions covering topics such as language support, non-formal education, communication, active ageing, and health. They will also receive training on safety, first aid, and volunteering ethics. Regular reflection and learning sessions will be promoted, with personalised monitoring and validation of skills through Youthpass.

•	Aged between 18 and 30;
•	Motivation to work with elderly people and participate in social causes;
•	Empathy, responsibility and good communication skills;
•	Team spirit and openness to multicultural contexts;
•	Interest in learning and developing personal and social skills;
•	Preferably young people with fewer opportunities (economic, geographical or social);
•	Commitment to the values of solidarity, inclusion and European citizenship;
•	No previous experience necessary - just availability, motivation and a willingness to contribute to the community.

