The volunteers at the Youth Center will support activities focused on developing youth initiatives, social inclusion, and non-formal education. They will take part in organizing creative workshops, eco and sports events, volunteer and sustainability campaigns, as well as supporting local communities. Volunteers will assist in the daily work of the center – welcoming visitors, maintaining common areas, preparing materials, and managing communication on social media. They will work in an international team, developing teamwork, leadership, and intercultural skills. The project will offer them the opportunity to express their ideas, implement small initiatives, and contribute to creating an inspiring environment where young people feel accepted, active, and engaged in the Rhodope community. Just 15 minutes from Smolyan, there is a ski resort, and the mountain offers plenty of opportunities for hiking and relaxation amidst beautiful nature.

The volunteers will work an average of 30 to 35 hours per week, with a total of 20 working and 10 free days. Meals will be provided during working days. Pocket money and food allowance amount to 205 EUR per month. Volunteers will be accommodated in a house in Smolyan, sharing rooms with other participants. Travel costs will be reimbursed up to a fixed maximum budget (between 180 and 410 EUR), depending on the means of transport and the distance calculated through the Erasmus+ distance calculator. Participants coming from less than 1000 km away will be encouraged to travel by bus or train.

During the opportunity, volunteers will take part in an introductory training covering the project’s goals, safety, cultural context, and daily tasks. They will join sessions on teamwork, communication, sustainability, and project management. Volunteers will also gain specific skills related to their activities – facilitating youth events, leading creative and environmental workshops, developing media literacy, and working with children and young people. At the end of the project, their acquired competences will be evaluated and recognized through a Youthpass certificate.

→ Aged between 18 and 30 years old;
→ Permanent residence in a country with no visa requirements for Bulgaria;
→ Volunteers with diverse backgrounds and experiences, including young people with fewer opportunities;
→ With a variety of interests and skills – sustainability, permaculture, event organization, project management, youth work, multimedia, etc.;
→ Willingness to live close to nature and adapt to basic living conditions (shared kitchen, solar shower, limited access to shops and services).

Volunteers will live and work in Smolyan, one of the most beautiful mountain towns in Bulgaria, as part of a dynamic international team engaged in youth and ecological initiatives.

📧 If you feel motivated to join, send your CV and a short motivation letter to: lora.abadjieva@gmail.com
Оur FB page: NC Future now

The Kaunas Municipal Vincas Kudirka Public Library, established in 1925, is a cornerstone of cultural and educational life in Kaunas, Lithuania's second-largest city. As one of the oldest municipal public libraries in the country, it has a rich history of serving the community. Our library, which now includes five functional departments and 20 branch libraries across the city, is dedicated to promoting literacy, lifelong learning, and cultural engagement.
We serve a diverse target group, including students, researchers, local residents, and visitors of all ages. Our values are rooted in accessibility, inclusivity, and community enrichment. We strive to create an open and welcoming environment where everyone can access a wealth of information, participate in cultural events, and engage in educational opportunities.

The volunteer will receive free accommodation during their stay and a private room in a shared apartment. You will have a monthly ticket for public transportation and monthly food and pocket money (280 euros/month).

* If needed, we can provide support and provide food products.

- Volunteering group meetings once a month;
- Meeting with a mentor once a month; 
- On-arrival and mid-term training;
- Online language learning;
- Participating in public solidarity events;
- Organization of info/promo solidarity events.

You are interested in working with children and young people. You are also a motivated and independent person.
*PLEASE SUBMIT YOUR CV AND MOTIVATIONAL LETTER IN ENGLISH*

EU.Motion 20.26 is a project by Associação Mais Cidadania, that aims to address two specific problems: 
- low participation rates of young people in decision-making processes;
- cultural integration and social exclusion.
Therefore, the project will develop activities connected with Citizenship, Participation, and Cultural Diversity.

With that in mind, we are looking for a motivated volunteer to join our office team for 8 months, taking an active role in the field of communication and digital media. The selected person will be fully involved in the organization’s daily life and all dimensions of AMC’s work. Their main focus will be on managing and creating digital content for our social media platforms (especially Facebook and Instagram), developing and implementing communication strategies for AMC’s projects, and designing promotional materials that reflect the organization’s identity. The volunteer will play a key role in shaping AMC’s online presence.

As established by the European Solidarity Corps, all volunteers have the right to accommodation, shared with other volunteers, pocket money and food allowance, as well as transportation.
At the beginning of each month, the volunteer will receive the pocket money in cash and, 5 to 7 days later, the food allowance.
Besides this, they will also acquire a monthly pass, allowing them to use all the public means of transportation (metro, train, tramway, and bus).

The volunteer will take part in all activities foreseen in the Volunteering Training and Evaluation Cycle in the Hosting Country and, in the Volunteering meetings proposed by the Sending Organisation and/or National Agencies.

The volunteer should be someone:
- highly motivated and proactive, with a strong background in digital communication;
- with experience in social media management, content creation, and video editing, and a genuine passion for storytelling;
- creative, flexible, and well-organized, able to adapt quickly to new challenges and environments;
- enthusiastic about living and working in a multicultural and cooperative setting;
- confident communicating and working in English, and open to learning Portuguese;
- eager to learn more about AMC’s work within the Non-Profit sector and contribute actively to its projects;
- willing to share ideas, skills, and personal interests with other young people, both online and offline.

The volunteer will develop, according to his/her competencies and knowledge, activities within the departments of AJD: Community School: - the volunteer will be involved in supporting the Community School, providing support to the monitors, and developing, under their guidance, the daily activities with children and young people (study time, arts, body language, science, computer, free time, etc.); - develop the AJD community garden; - rethinking AJD's outdoor space with stimuli for learning by playing through non-formal education; - develop ideas to make the Playroom more "Green". Communication and Image Department - the volunteer will receive adequate language training and he/she will contribute to the blog; There will also be the chance to go to schools, elderly centres, the volunteer will go weekly for a 2-hour shift to help the Refood organization.

INFOPACK: https://drive.google.com/file/d/16F4tUxQeXjvV70ztBLHsA44oCDBCyuf7/view?usp=sharing

Pocket Money for the period of activity has an amount of 6 euros per day. 
Meals: the amount for lunch or lunch on working days will be provided by AJD. For other lunches, dinners, breakfasts and snacks the volunteer will be given the value of EUR 125,00 per month, by bank transfer. 
Accommodation: shared house for volunteers. AJD will be responsible for the payment of the monthly rent and expenses, including the internet. Travel on public transport: a monthly bus pass, which is required for journeys between the accommodation and the local activities, will be provided. Bicycles are provided.

Upon arrival, AJD will provide an on arrival short training/welcoming, in which the volunteers will be introduced to the organization, their tasks, etc. 
Later, volunteers will attend an on-arrival training and later a mid-term training with the Portuguese National Agency. 
Similarly, during the performance of his/her tasks, the volunteer will receive support, guidance and supervision from the monitor/supervisor who is responsible for each activity. The host/coordinating organisation will ensure that volunteers have free language training throughout the whole service.

Volunteers must:
- be open-minded, respect others, be willing to get out of the comfort zone, be ready to be in the rural area for the activities at AJD, be motivated to learn Portuguese and interact with others;
- have an interest and will to work with children and young people;
- have an interest and will to work with old people;
- have an interest and will to work with people with social obstacles (different ethnicities);
- be interested in preserving the environment. It is necessary to continue the project of the association's community garden;
- have an interest in communication, design, blogging and social media;
- it is also valuable to have good communication skills and the will to organize events for the community.

This European Solidarity Corps team volunteering project invites young people from across Europe to come together in Vermil village, Guimarães, Portugal, for a transformative experience that blends ecology, creativity and community action.
During two weeks in the end of March and beginning of April 2026, volunteers will join forces with local residents and the CAISA team to revive green spaces, promote environmental awareness, and use art as a tool for regeneration. Through collective work, shared learning and intercultural exchange, participants will rediscover the power of collaboration — and awaken a shared sense of responsibility for our planet.

Volunteers will be hosted in a shared accommodation provided by CAISA, located in a peaceful area close to our activity spaces.
Participants will share rooms divided by gender, with access to a fully equipped kitchen, living room, bathroom, and a large outdoor area — including a sports field right next door.
All basic facilities are included: Wi-Fi, heating, water, electricity, bed linen, and towels.
Volunteers will receive a pocket money allowance of 6€ per day.
Meals are provided, and cooking is done in teams, following a rotation system. We prepare three meals per day and eat together.

During the Re-Green project, volunteers will receive ongoing training and support to help them fully engage in the activities and develop new skills. The training will include:
Introduction and Orientation;
Environmental Awareness;
Teamwork and Project Skills;
Practical Skills for Activities;
Reflection and Intercultural Learning.
All training is practical, interactive, and tailored to help volunteers gain personal, professional, and intercultural competences while contributing meaningfully to the project and the local community.

We are looking for motivated, creative and environmentally conscious volunteers who want to make a positive impact in the community while living an unforgettable intercultural experience in Portugal.
The Re-Green project is for people who:
Care about nature, sustainability and community life;
Enjoy working outdoors and don’t mind getting their hands dirty;
Are interested in upcycling, gardening, eco-art or creative reuse;
Love teamwork, intercultural exchange and learning by doing;
Are open-minded, flexible and ready to contribute with ideas and energy.
🌿 What you’ll do
As a Re-Green volunteer, you’ll be part of a team helping to:
Restore and reimagine green community spaces;
Create art installations and environmental awareness campaigns;
Support local workshops on circular economy and sustainability;
Engage with children, youth and seniors through creative and ecological activities.
🌎 Ideal volunteer profile
You don’t need to be an expert — just curious, proactive and passionate about the planet.
If you enjoy connecting with people, creating something meaningful together, and believe that art and nature can transform communities, this project is for you.

The volunteer will develop, according to his/her competencies and knowledge, activities within the departments of AJD: Community School: - the volunteer will be involved in supporting the Community School, providing support to the monitors, and developing, under their guidance, the daily activities with children and young people (study time, arts, body language, science, computer, free time, etc.); - develop the AJD community garden; - rethinking AJD's outdoor space with stimuli for learning by playing through non-formal education; - develop ideas to make the Playroom more "Green". Communication and Image Department - the volunteer will receive adequate language training and he/she will contribute to the blog; Project Department: - support in project work and meetings with partners, preparation of activities, etc. There will also be the chance to go to schools, elderly centres, etc.

Infopack: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dzbM6KI2pRkusv5WwZKCxClYgHzgCh8x/view?usp=sharing

Pocket Money for the period of activity has an amount of 6 euros per day. 
Meals: the amount for lunch or lunch on working days will be provided by AJD. For other lunches, dinners, breakfasts and snacks the volunteer will be given the value of EUR 125,00 per month, by bank transfer. 
Accommodation: shared house for volunteers. AJD will be responsible for the payment of the monthly rent and expenses, including the internet. Travel on public transport: a monthly bus pass, which is required for journeys between the accommodation and the local activities, will be provided. Bicycles are provided.

Upon arrival, AJD will provide an on arrival short training/welcoming, in which the volunteers will be introduced to the organization, their tasks, etc. 
Later, volunteers will attend an on-arrival training and later a mid-term training with the Portuguese National Agency. 
Similarly, during the performance of his/her tasks, the volunteer will receive support, guidance and supervision from the monitor/supervisor who is responsible for each activity. The host/coordinating organisation will ensure that volunteers have free language training throughout the whole service.

Volunteers must:
- be open-minded, respect others, be willing to get out of the comfort zone, be ready to be in the rural area for the activities at AJD, be motivated to learn Portuguese and interact with others;
- have an interest and will to work with children and young people;
- have an interest and will to work with old people;
- have an interest and will to work with people with social obstacles (different ethnicities);
- be interested in preserving the environment. It is necessary to continue the project of the association's community garden;
- have an interest in communication, design, blogging and social media;
- it is also valuable to have good communication skills and the will to organize events for the community.

Seeking to raise awareness on environmental issues and sustainability, to promote eco-citizenship, as well as intergenerational and intercultural dialogue, in the rural community of Caumont-sur-Aure, the Collège Les Sources d’Aure wishes to cooperate with a young European volunteer on the following missions : 
-	Creation and animation of activities on the thematics of culture, sustainability and eco-citizenship for a variety of publics ;
-	Work on the creation of intergenerational bridges ;
-	Promotion of linguistic exchange and interculturality ; 
-	Co-organisation of local events ; 
This mission includes multiple structures, such as the local Middle School, the Media Library that also includes the media museum, the Youth Center and a social, cultural and youth association, all open to people of all ages, while the Leisure Center to children from 3 to 12 years old. The volunteer will cooperate with each structure, sharing their ideas and proposing activities to be implemented.

The volunteer will have an individual room in an appartment located in the middle school of Caumont, shared with a young assistant of english language. The volunteer will be responsible for the preparation of their own meals, while beeing provided with a free lunch from the school’s canteen on Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday and Friday. A bike will be provided to the volunteer to support the transport in Caumont and between the different activity sites. A carpooling option is available to ensure access to neighboring towns, such as Caen or Vire. A bus also connecting Caumont to the city of Caen.

- Participation in an arrival and mid-term formation concerning ESC volunteers, proposed by the French National Agency ;
- Participation on training courses, proposed by Europe Direct thanks to a partnership wiht the Départment, on the thematics of Europe, citizenship, democratic life, etc. and different educational practices (academic, adapted and non-formal education) ;

We are looking for a curious, autonomous, social and creative person, who is interested in sustainable development and eco-friendly practices, in raising awareness and who values intergenerational exchange and interculturality. The volunteer should feel confortable living in a small rural town, such as Caumont. Lastly, the knowledge of French is not obligatory, though appreciated.

With this project, we aim at a cross-culture bridge between the Roma and non- Roma young people which will set an example of fruitful cooperation, inclusion and responsibility for other people, communities and countries. You will have individual as well as team activities. 
The activities will comprise a series of workshops that you, with our full support, will organize and hold for adolescents on varied topics (personal development, ESC and Erasmus+ opportunities, workshops on health and environment, freedom of expression through arts, handicrafts, Civic Education, Rights and Responsibilities Workshops, etc).
There will be some office activities as well as outside the office ones.  
The atmosphere will be engaging, creative and you  will have the chance to express your creative and artistic sides, a project of your own and also learn and provide information through non-formal methods.

The association will provide: 1. transportation money (from the volunteers’ countries to Iasi, Romania) 2. visa costs  3. accommodation with house expenses covered  4. pocket money 5. Money for food 
Pocket Money -120 eur/month Food Allowance -160 eur/month 
We provide accommodation in a fully quipped and furnished apartment. Rent and utilities (gas, electricity) will be paid by the hosting NGO.

The volunteers will receive orientation and support throughout the process and for the activities as well as a mentor, a coordinator and Romanian classes.

- are young people between 18 and 30 years old;
- have a real desire to spend almost a year in Romani;
- have good social and communications skills;
- are flexible, willing to learn and help the others;
- are able to take initiatives and propose their ideas;
- are open-minded and enthusiastic;
- have knowledge of the English language (level A2 - B1);
- believe in the volunteering work and want to contribute to improving it;
- have a minimum experience of volunteering/working with teenagers/minorities;
- feel comfortable working with teenagers between 14 and 19 years old;
- are interested in developing and spreading the spirit of civic involvment;
 - want to learn Romanian, as it will be necessary in some of the activities;
- want to discover new cultures, traditions and ways of living;
- are motivated to learn competences for a future job: our focus will be on social work, minorities, culture and non-formal education;
- are responsible and willing to share their culture and knowledge with the target groups;
- have a positive attitude.
- Important: artistic/creative skills: music and dance, pottery, crafts - weaving, knitting, painting; technical skills - IT

Step into the world of Actio Catholica Patria, a youth organization that has been igniting passions since 1991 in Lithuania. With a mission to nurture resilient, independent individuals, we believe in fostering a sense of belonging and purpose within our community. At the heart of our mission is the Open Youth Centre "Vartai," where young people aged 14-29 can embark on a journey of self-discovery and growth, regardless of their background. "Vartai" is a space free from violence, bullying, and negativity, where creativity knows no bounds. Picture yourself immersed in different activities, from board games to outdoor adventures, and unleash your inner artist in our various workshops. With unwavering support and guidance, "Vartai" is a place to empower the young to not only succeed as an individual but also flourish as an integral members of society.

You will receive a private room in a shared flat with other international volunteers, a public transport card, monthly food and pocket money (~250 eu).

*If needed, we can provide support and provide food products. 

*PLEASE SUBMIT YOUR CV AND MOTIVATIONAL LETTER IN ENGLISH*

- Volunteering group meetings once a month;
- Meeting with a mentor once a month; 
- On-arrival and mid-term training;
- Online language learning;
- Participating in public solidarity events;
- Organization of info/promo solidarity events.

Embark on an exhilarating journey as a volunteer, poised to forge meaningful connections with the youngins at the Open Youth Center! Harness the power of creativity and reflection as working in this dynamic team. Dive deep into the world of youth, understanding their unique perspectives and backgrounds.  Here, innovation is your compass, and every idea is a potential bridge to equal and respectful relationships with these incredible young minds. Take up a volunteering role where you will not only participate in the organization of open evenings but also craft and execute engaging activities.

The hosting organisation, the Institut Royal pour les Handicapés de l’Ouie et de la Vue (IRHOV), comprises two specialised schools for youth aged 3 to 21 with visual and hearing impairments. IRHOV is dedicated to innovative projects in both formal and non-formal education, incorporating sports and cultural activities tailored to the needs of those with sensory impairments.

During the volunteering experience at IRHOV, the volunteer will engage in various activities for students and their families. Key roles will include:
•	Supporting and organising extracurricular activities such as sports days, theatre, and reading sessions;
•	Enhancing connections between families and strengthening community bonds within the school;
•	Raising awareness about visual impairment and supporting others in understanding the barriers and challenges faced by persons with visual impairments;
•	Promoting a positive image of visual impairment to students from mainstream schools to foster inclusivity.

The volunteers' apartment features two bedrooms and a spacious shared living area. Volunteers will either have a private room or share with another young person, with shared kitchen, bathroom, and toilet facilities. The apartment is equipped with tactile markers on appliances, contrasting tableware, and labelled storage boxes to ensure ease of use and accessibility.

Located in the vibrant Sainte-Marguerite neighbourhood of Liège, the area offers opportunities for independence, supported by mobility and orientation classes.

During their first two weeks, visually impaired volunteers will receive orientation training, as well as sessions on daily living and professional skills. The schedule for these sessions will be arranged in agreement with supervisors, taking into consideration individual needs and preferences. Intensive French classes will also be provided during this period, using adapted materials and taught by a specialised instructor with extensive experience teaching visually impaired students.

We are seeking visually impaired individuals aged between 18 and 30 with a beginner level of French (A2). If you are motivated, eager to be actually involved in the working team, and strive for autonomy in your daily life, you are a perfect fit for this ESC project. Essential qualities include openness, good listening skills, and a genuine desire to make a positive impact.

Promote health and social transformation trough outdoor sport, namely surf and sustainability education. Volunteers will be involved in supporting the SCV's managing Surfingviana High Performance Center in administrative tasks, coachs in surf and bodyboard school carrying out the different daily activities, namely with young, elder and people with special needs, university camps, national and international events and in many other activities that help to develop better health and wellbeing and improvement of athletes. Support the facilities reception, Check lists; distribution of sports equipment support in the control orientation facilities, distribution of sports equipment, beach and water surf practice support, housekeeping and cleaning spaces, and in general supporting, planning and accompaniment of all activities. Improve sustainable plan and provide the participation themselves of promoting healthy lifestyle and physical activity.

Pocket money - 5€/day - and monthly allowance - 4€/day - are payed monthly. 
Accommodation in individual or shared room and free access to all facilities (shared spaces, kitchen, WCs and balcony) in a house close to the Surfingviana HPC. 
Travel from residence country and transports from and to the activity expenses are reimbursed to the volunteer in the first month of payment if presented.
Transport from and to the Surfingviana HPC, can be provided by car ride with SCV workers or can be done walking or riding a bicycle.

Welcome and training on arrival in the organization before start the activity.
Training with organization coaches.
Daily workers acompaignment; participations in trainings, projects and experiences with other institutions.
On arrival and midterm training leading by Portugal National Agency.
Mentorship provided.
Portuguese course and other trainings needed provided by the organization.

Willingness and availability to work, learn and help; 
Responsability, creativity, autonomy, ease of interpersonal relations and teamwork, determination, empathy, dynamism, initiative, ability to manage unforeseeable situations and elementary loyalty to the SCV; 
Deal different groups, nationalities, ages and special needs; 
Flexibility to perform different tasks and dynamic schedules; 
Speak English; 
Interest of sport and motivation for physical activity in outdoor, sports, sustainability and tourism; 
Networking ability.
Person with fewer oportunities (long last unemployment; geographic or economic or cultural obstacles)

IBO is an NGO based in Ferrara and Parma, Italy. Its mission is to promote access to education as a fundamental right for every person, especially children and youth from disadvantaged communities. This aim is carried out through a wide range of projects, from volunteering to international cooperation in the field of education and training, in Italy and worldwide (Africa, Latin America, etc.) 
We are looking for a volunteer who want to support us in these activities: 
- organizing and carrying out workshops in local schools about environment, migration and inequalities;
-organization and participation in fundraising campaigns and events;
-promotion of social and awareness-raising events in the area; 
- support in the creation and promotion of information material; 
- support in the communication area (management of the IBO Parma FB page). 
Dates are a bit flexible. If you meet the requirements, apply for the opportunity and we will invite you to an online meeting.

This project does not include accommodation and food. The ideal candidate is someone who already resides in Parma or in the surrounding areas and cities who can reach the place of the activities on a daily basis. The office is located inside the Co-working "On-Off", where you will have the opportunity to meet a lot of other people. The activities also take place outside the office, such as in local schools and other social places. 
What we offer: monthly pocket money, insurance, youth pass certificate.
What we ask: 30 service hours a week.

We offer volunteers the opportunity to attend these face-to-face trainings: one arrival general training about IBO, arrival and mid term trainings organized by our National Agency for Youth, and other eventual trainings and workshops depending on the period.

Requirements:
- Residing in Parma or surrounding territories/cities;
- Advanced knowledge of Italian language;
- Knowledge of English language is preferable; 
- Experience in group coordination or in the socio-educational field is preferable;
- Experience in organizing events or campaigns is preferable; 
- Experience in using multimedia tools is preferable.

The social care center "Vija" is a budgetary institution, that provides social care for disabled children and young people, left without parental care or lacking the basic skills to live independently. The volunteer would aim to create a comfortable and safe home-like environment for children and adults, seeking to protect the rights and interests of our clients. You would also aid in developing our client's ability to take care of themselves and help our clients integrate successfully into society. We also need help organizing and carrying out various activities with client groups (board games, sports activities, music therapy, etc.) and also various outdoor activities with clients (walking, playing outdoor games). You can work alongside our employees and assist the occupational therapist of our care home (dog therapy, handicrafts, etc.).

The volunteer will receive free accommodation for the duration of their stay, with a private room in a shared apartment. In addition, participants will be provided with a monthly allowance for food and pocket money, approximately 250 euros per month. To support local travel, volunteers will also receive a monthly public transportation ticket, fully covered by the project.

During the opportunity, volunteers will take part in various training and development activities aimed at enhancing their experience and skills. These include monthly group meetings with fellow volunteers to share insights and build teamwork, as well as monthly one-on-one sessions with a mentor for personal support. Participants will also attend on-arrival and mid-term training sessions, have access to online language learning tools, and take part in public solidarity events to engage with the wider community.

You would like to spend time with children and young people with disabilities;
You are not afraid of challenges;
You are an empathetic person;
You are a team player!

SCI Italy's project “La Città dell'Utopia” started in 2003 and it is located in the neighborhood of San Paolo (via Valeriano 3F – Rome), a popular suburban area inhabited mainly by elderly people, university students, and migrant families coming from Latin America, northeastern Europe, Asia, and Africa. The building is used to host several groups and associations working on active citizenships, especially in relation to migration, environmental sustainability, antifascism, gender, and self-determination of food and consumption.
The main activities carried out in “La Città dell’Utopia” are:

Organizing and hosting of international workcamps, trainings, and international youth meetings.
Organizing and running awareness-raising events.
Organizing meetings, festivals, exhibitions, thematic meals, farmers’ markets, and courses on music, group dancing, language courses, gardening. 
Read the full call: https://sci-italia.it/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Call-LCU-ESC-26-27.pdf

In a separate flat in “La Città dell’Utopia”, with 3 shared double rooms (up to six international volunteers) kitchen, living room, and bathroom. The accommodation has all the basic facilities (Wi-Fi and washing machine included). The building is historic, so the accommodation is basic. There is no centralized heating or aircon, so it can be humid, cold in the winter, but also perfectly fresh in the summer. The building is surrounded by a very beautiful garden (which means mosquitos in the summer). It is located in a student area close to the metro.

The daily program consists of 6 hours 5 days a week. There will be 2 consecutive free days/ week and 2 days of holiday for each month. To
facilitate the participation of a high number of volunteers, some activities will take place during the weekend. In these cases, the number of working hours done by the volunteer will be adjusted for the following weeks, by reducing working hour’s amount o taking days off so that the total number of working hours per week does not exceed 35h.

Requirements:
good command of English;
being able to work in a team;
good communication skills and motivation to cooperate with your colleagues and the activists of “La Città dell’Utopia” and Servizio Civile Internazionale;
motivated to learn and share knowledge and skills;
good computer skills (Microsoft Office, email, graphic software);
being responsible and proactive and take initiative towards their tasks;
organizational skills;
good educational and social skills to be able to work with several target groups;
open mind and flexible attitude towards working hours;
Interest in activism and political awareness;

Preferable skills:
good command of the Italian language
basic administrative skills
webmastering or basic use of wordpress
previous experience in social network communication;

The activity will take place at the Maison Familiale et Rurale Centre Yonne which is a rural school welcoming students weekly. Younsgters are training to work in agricultural/farming and outdoor jobs. The volunteer will have a couple missions including:
> Raising awareness of locals about European mobility:
Take part in groups mobility ;
Implement actions to promote mobility experiences (film, photo, exhibition) for young people, families and internship supervisors;
> Promotion of European cultures and interculturality: 
Participate in or develop innovative departure preparations;
Organise activities about home country (meals, games, sports activity) or other cultures;
> Participation in the daily life of the House:
Organise activities in the evening for the younsters staying at the boarding school;
Accompany young people in educational activities at the MFR or outside;
Participation in Boards of Directors and communication actions (open house, forum, fair / party, etc.)

The volunteer will stay in a single room in the boarding school of the Maison Familiale and Rurale (washing machine, dryer, kitchen available at the MFR). 
Being in a rural area, the volunteer will have access to a car and there is a train Station 5 mins walking from the MFR.

Arrival and mid-term seminars organized by French National Agency
First aid training
Participate in training, seminars offered by the MFR network

We are looking for a dynamic and voluntary person with curiosity and strength of proposal. As we are in a rural area, the volunteer will need to be an active persone that likes nature and spending time outside.
The volunteer will work in a team and in contact of youngsters, therefore, a liking for team work and youth will be required.
REQUIRE DRIVING LICENCE

Current interventions of MdM in Sierra Leone focus on reducing Sexual and Reproductive Health (SRH) problems by strengthening the public health system, raising community awareness, and advocating for improved governance with a gender-sensitive approach. 
The volunteer will be based in Koinadugu particularly Kabala town, and will work closely with the Admin/Finance Officer. Tasks: Support the Sierra Leonean National team in financial administration and management and controlling (budget, accounting, reporting, and administrative HR procedures, etc.) in accordance with MdM policies and procedures; Strengthen the skills of the support team (Finance) in applying MdM policies and guidelines; Prepare, monitor, and update project and organizational budgets, ensuring alignment with donor requirements; Support uploading financial documents and filling MDM tools (Postbacking,..etc); Monitor expenditure against budgets, identify variances, and propose corrective actions.

Kabala is a calm and relatively safe town, offering a peaceful environment for work and daily life. The general atmosphere is friendly, and the community is welcoming. The work will take place at the MdM Sierra Leone base office that is located at Koinadugu district. The volunteer will then be accommodated in the organization's guesthouse. The volunteer will regularly receive information, support, & materials (laptop & phone) and transportation necessary for performing the functions assigned to them. You will receive a monthly subsistence allowance of 487€ to cover basic personal needs.

Volunteers will improve their professional knowledge through training in humanitarian action, and specific issues on security, gender, psychosocial support and will be provided with training resources to continue their learning. Those selected will receive briefings/training at MdM headquarters in Madrid with the different departments related to the mission and the position, as well as mandatory online training on security before they start their field work. Training sessions will take place both in the countries of the support organisations and host organisations.

EDUCATION
•	Bachelor's degree + 5 in economics and/or Bachelor's degree + 3 in administration/accounting;
•	Master's degree in development cooperation or similar;
EXPERIENCE
•	Experience in administrative and/or financial management of private and/or public organizations;
•	Knowledge of funding instruments and donor guidelines, and project cycle management;
•	Experience or additional training in strategy definition, project formulation, implementation, monitoring, evaluation, and capitalization;
•	Experience in the field of international cooperation is an asset;
•	Contextual knowledge of Africa is an asset;
SKILLS
•	Knowledge of basic administrative / financial procedures;
ACCOUNTANCY
•	Knowledge of auditing or internal control;
•	Knowledge of donor regulations;
•	Analytical skills to propose innovative strategies or approaches;
•	Ability to work in an organized environment and manage priorities, under high professional pressure;
•	Dynamism, initiative, autonomy, and respect for rules;
•	Courtesy, open-mindedness, and flexibility; a sense of humor is essential;
•	Computer skills (qualifications or certifications in some of the following applications are recommended);
•	Standard Microsoft tools: Windows, MS Office;
•	Data analysis and statistics: MS Excel;
LANGUAGES
•	English B2 or C1.
Eligibility : Candidates must be 18 to 35 years old, reside in one of the eligible countries (EU Member State, North Macedonia, Iceland, Liechtenstein or Turkey), have completed the compulsory Humanitarian Aid Volunteering training and not have participated before in individual Humanitarian Aid Volunteering. When adding together this new volunteering opportunity and any previous participation in EU volunteering programmes, the total duration cannot exceed 12 months.

ENGIM in collaboration with AmaZOOnico - dedicated to rehabilitation and reinsertion of wild animals confiscated from illegal trade - seeks to protect and preserve the amazon forest as an ecosystem, by also addressing humans and animals communities living in there. Through conservation, education, and community engagement, the project aims to enhance the work of the staff to raise awareness about biodiversity protection and promote sustainable coexistence.
The volunteer will support in the following activities: Assisting with the daily care of animals – feeding, cleaning and developing care protocols; Guiding tours for visitors and tourists to raise awareness about wildlife illegal trafficking and the importance of environmental conservation; Helping with the general maintenance of the center; Coordinating, programming and delivering English classes for adults (local staff) and children of the surrounding communities; Supporting daily administrative and communication tasks.

Volunteers will be accommodated in a guesthouse for volunteers in the rescue center. Basic utilities such as electricity, water, and internet will be available, though service may be intermittent due to contingencies. A monthly allowance of €700 will be provided, covering daily expenses and local transport. Food will be provided directly by the AmaZOOnico and shared with the other volunteers hosted at the facility. A laptop will be provided, and reimbursement for mobile phone expenses is included.Flexible working hours, including working on weekends, may be requested depending on the schedule.

Pre-departure training on humanitarian principles, security, and program-specific knowledge;
Pre-departure training on political and cultural Ecuadorian context;
On-site training on wildlife conservation, illegal trafficking, biosecurity, and intercultural approaches;
Access to training resources for continuous learning;
Regular briefings with ENGIM's technical and social staff;

We are looking for a motivated person willing to live in a rural, isolated area with limited leisure opportunities. The candidate should be flexible and open to a multicultural environment, as they will be surrounded by many other volunteers and expected to share common living spaces. The location presents certain security challenges, which require a modest lifestyle and strict adherence to safety protocols. A genuine interest in fieldwork is essential, along with the ability to adapt to demanding and unpredictable weather conditions. We are particularly seeking someone that, besides having a strong interest in wildlife and environmental conservation, has very good language skills and preferably a degree in languages or experience in teaching English to adults. 
Education & Training: Degree or background in languages, education, environmental sciences, or related fields; Experience teaching English to adults and/or children is an asset; Additional knowledge in environmental education, wildlife conservation and community development is highly valued.
Skills & Competencies: Strong interpersonal and intercultural communication skills; Willingness to work in rural areas and within multidisciplinary teams;  Proactivity, adaptability, and problem-solving attitude.
Language & Technical Skills: Good knowledge of Spanish (minimum level B2); Proficiency in English;
Eligibility: Candidates must be 18 to 35 years old, reside in one of the eligible countries (EU Member State, North Macedonia, Iceland, Liechtenstein or Turkey), have completed the compulsory Humanitarian Aid Volunteering training and not have participated before in individual Humanitarian Aid Volunteering. When adding together this new volunteering opportunity and any previous participation in EU volunteering programmes, the total duration cannot exceed 12 months.

The ultimate goal of this project is to create a community ecological garden, based on the principles of permaculture. As such, the volunteer will be required to participate in manual work related to the preparation and maintenance of the garden. These activities will take place exclusively in the morning, ensuring that the volunteer has free time after lunch to enjoy the cultural and personal experience provided by the project.

Santarém is a historic city with over a thousand years of history, located in the center of Portugal and bordered by the Tagus River, the largest river in the Iberian Peninsula. It has around 60,000 inhabitants and enjoys a strategic location: 60 km from Lisbon, 50 km from the Atlantic Ocean, 200 km from both Porto and the Algarve, and 120 km from the Spanish border. The city is well served by public transport, with regular train and bus connections, ensuring easy access and mobility.

P.S. The activity will be at least 150 days.

Volunteers will be accommodated in a renovated 500-year-old palace located in the historic center of Santarém. The residence includes a kitchen, private bathroom, dining room, living room, cinema room, games room (with pool table and board games), bar, and an interior courtyard of approximately 100m2.

Travel, meals and health insurance will be covered by the organisation.
The volunteer will also be given a weekly allowance.

Participants will receive introductory training on the activities to be carried out. The volunteer will be guided, trained, and supported by the project coordinator through direct supervision and hands-on learning. All activities are carefully planned to ensure the safety and well-being of all participants.
To support, reinforce, and complement the learning acquired through participation, specific quality and support measures will be implemented, such as the online general training, the training and evaluation cycle, ongoing mentoring, and formal recognition of the learning outcomes achieved.

We are looking for volunteers who:
❑ Are between 18 and 30 years old;
❑ Are motivated to work as part of a team, proactive and flexible;
❑ Prepared to develop socio-cultural, environmental and sporting activities and develop their own activities;
❑ Have an interest or experience in environmental issues, sustainable buildings and take part in activities for the community;
❑ Every participant should speak at least basic English and stay open to other people, respect their culture and habits;
❑ Participants will learn Portuguese according to their motivation;
❑ The project has a clear structure, but we are also totally open to ideas that may arise before and during the project, and we are also able to adapt the volunteers'motivations to our reality in order to better manage their motivations and get the most out of their experience and perspectives.

The ultimate goal of this project is to create a community ecological garden, based on the principles of permaculture. As such, the volunteer will be required to participate in manual work related to the preparation and maintenance of the garden. These activities will take place exclusively in the morning, ensuring that the volunteer has free time after lunch to enjoy the cultural and personal experience provided by the project.
