To support, reinforce, and complement the learning acquired through participation, specific quality and support measures will be implemented, such as the online general training, the training and evaluation cycle, ongoing mentoring, and formal recognition of the learning outcomes achieved.

We are looking for volunteers who:
❑ Are between 18 and 30 years old;
❑ Are motivated to work as part of a team, proactive and flexible;
❑ Prepared to develop socio-cultural, environmental and sporting activities and develop their own activities;
❑ Have an interest or experience in environmental issues, sustainable buildings and take part in activities for the community;
❑ Every participant should speak at least basic English and stay open to other people, respect their culture and habits;
❑ Participants will learn Portuguese according to their motivation;
❑ The project has a clear structure, but we are also totally open to ideas that may arise before and during the project, and we are also able to adapt the volunteers'motivations to our reality in order to better manage their motivations and get the most out of their experience and perspectives.

ENGIM has been active in Ecuador since 2005, promoting the integral development of vulnerable communities.
The project operates in the WASH sector to ensure sustainable access to drinking water through participatory design and construction of community aqueducts.
The volunteer will support the technical team mainly in fieldwork and manual tasks:
- carrying out surveys, collecting topographic data, mapping and verifying water sources;
- supporting the design and implementation of aqueducts in rural and indigenous areas;
- engaging in manual activities such as pipe transport and installation, trench digging, material handling, and filtration setup;
- assisting in community mingas, motivating participation and working alongside local people;
- contributing to the creation and training of Water Committees for sustainable management;
- helping with logistics such as material preparation, transport, storage, and tool management.

Volunteers will be accommodated in a shared apartment or guesthouse in a community near the project area. Basic utilities such as electricity, water, and internet access will be available, though service may be intermittent due to contingencies.
A monthly allowance of €800 will be provided, covering daily expenses, food and local transport.
A laptop will be provided, and reimbursement for mobile phone expenses is included.
Flexible working hours and a combination of on-site and remote work may be available, depending on the autonomy of the volunteer and the schedule of activities.

Pre-departure training on humanitarian principles, security, and program-specific knowledge
Pre-departure training on political and cultural Ecuadorian context
On-site training on WASH systems, community water management, technical tools, and intercultural approaches
Access to training resources for continuous learning
Regular briefings with ENGIM's technical and social staff

We are looking for a motivated person willing to live in Tena, a small city known as the gateway to the Amazon region. The living conditions are simpe, with access to essential services, markets, and leisure opportunities. While a modest lifestyle and respect for local customs are expected, the security situation is relatively stable and less challenging. The position requires a strong inclination for fieldwork in surrounding rural and indigenous communities, often in hot and humid climates, with activities carried out in outdoor and sometimes physically demanding conditions.
Degree or technical training in Environmental Engineering, Civil Engineering, Geology, Architecture, International Development or similar fields;

Additional training in WASH, water resource management, or community participation is an asset.
Basic technical knowledge in water systems and project management;
Strong interpersonal and intercultural communication skills;
Willingness to work in rural areas and within multidisciplinary teams;

Proactivity, adaptability, and problem-solving attitude.
Good knowledge of Spanish (minimum level B2);
Basic knowledge of technical tools and software (e.g., AutoCAD, QGIS, Excel).

Proficiency in MS Office / Google Workspace; familiarity with KoboToolbox or similar data‑collection apps desirable
Candidates must be 18 to 35 years old, reside in one of the eligible countries (EU Member State, North Macedonia, Iceland, Liechtenstein or Turkey), have completed the compulsory Humanitarian Aid Volunteering training and not have participated before in individual Humanitarian Aid Volunteering. When adding together this new volunteering opportunity and any previous participation in EU volunteering programmes, the total duration cannot exceed 12 months.

ENGIM is implementing the SkillAlb project in Albania to strengthen youth employability and foster inclusive growth. The initiative focuses on vocational schools and training centres, while also supporting teachers and youth workers through training and guidance.
The volunteer will support the team in Fier, contributing to the visibility of ENGIM’s initiatives by:
Creating engaging content for digital campaigns (social media posts, newsletters, reports);
Producing graphic and visual materials (infographics, photos, short videos) to showcase activities, impact and stories;
Updating the project website and social channels, monitoring engagement and proposing new strategies;
Supporting the organisation of events, workshops and public presentations (logistics, materials, promotion);
Drafting communication guidelines, partner materials and project reports;
Collecting testimonies and interviews with youth participants, teachers and stakeholders.

Volunteers will be accommodated in a shared apartment with other expats. Electricity, cold and hot water (not potable), internet, equipped kitchen and washing machine available in the apartment. A monthly subsistence allowance of 800€ will be provided to cover basic needs, food and local transport. Flexible working hours and a combination of on-site and remote work may be available, depending on the autonomy of the volunteer and the schedule of activities.

Pre-departure training on local context, ongoing programs, humanitarian principles and security.
On-site and pre-departure training on community engagement, intercultural approach, communication in the non-profit sector.
Learning in the workplace in a multicultural and multidisciplinary team. 
The volunteer will receive briefings/training with different departments related to the mission and the position.

Education & Training: - Degree in Communication Sciences, Marketing, Social Media Management, or similar fields. - Experience in using social media management tools and/or website management. - Experience in audiovisual production (filming, editing). Skills & Competencies: - Excellent writing skills, with the ability to communicate clearly and persuasively. - Teamwork skills and ability to work in multicultural environments. - Organizational and problem-solving skills. - Autonomy and ability to manage priorities. Desirable Skills - Graphic design skills. - Interest in international cooperation and solidarity. Language & Technical Skills:: - Proficiency in Spanish (preferably B2 level or higher) - Basic knowledge of Microsoft Office, Google suite, Wordpress Candidates must be 18 to 35 years old, reside in one of the eligible countries (EU Member State, North Macedonia, Iceland, Liechtenstein or Turkey), have completed the compulsory Humanitarian Aid Volunteering training and not have participated before in individual Humanitarian Aid Volunteering. When adding together this new volunteering opportunity and any previous participation in EU volunteering programmes, the total duration cannot exceed 12 months.

“Volunteering in Lousã: Local Development Project” aims to promote community engagement and solidarity through local actions that connect generations and cultures. Volunteers will support activities for children, youth, and elderly people, contribute to cultural and non-formal education initiatives, and assist Activar’s departments in communication, tourism, and event organization. The project encourages active citizenship, intercultural learning, and personal growth while strengthening the social fabric of Lousã. By combining daily community work with creative and educational initiatives, volunteers will play a key role in fostering inclusion, participation, and sustainable local development.

You will have a single or double bedroom in a fully equipped flat in the centre of Lousã, with access to services nearby: bakeries, supermarkets, cafes, pubs, pharmacies, health centre; post office, swimming pool, gym, nature and cultural spaces. Food allowance will be given monthly. There are local public transports and a bus to the city of Coimbra. You will be able to reach the workplaces and main services by bike or on foot and might also use Activar's van punctually for long-distance activities.

Regular meetings and integration in Activar's teams as well as "on the job" training will be provided. You will be given access to Online Linguistic Support (OLS) platform and we will also suggest other tools to study and learn the portuguese language. Support for clarifying doubts and motivation to improve your skills and develop your ideas will be given by the kindergarten/youth office workers, the ESC coordinator and the mentor. You will also be enrolled on the On-arrival training provided by Portuguese National Agency.

We are looking for a motivated young person who wants to be part of the life of a beautiful, authentic Portuguese village and experience local culture up close.

The volunteer should:
Enjoy working with children, youth, and elderly people;
Be flexible and ready to help in workshops, events, cultural activities, tourism, and community projects;
Bring energy, curiosity, and a positive attitude, open to new experiences and different cultures;
Have creative skills (painting, singing, playing an instrument, handcrafts) — a big plus;
Speak or want to learn/improve Portuguese.

No prior experience is needed — just motivation, curiosity, and a willingness to join the local community life!

Le Centre Socio-Culturel Jean Wagner œuvre depuis 1964 au développement social des quartiers prioritaires de la Ville de Mulhouse, facilitant l’autonomisation des jeunes à travers ses activités de gestionnaire de crèche, de périscolaire, d’activités extrascolaires, animation jeunesse, le développement du pouvoir d’agir et de la citoyenneté des habitants. 
Les missions qui seront confiées aux volontaires seront tutorées par des professionnels expérimentés dans le domaine de l’animation socio-éducative: 
1. Accompagner les enfants en difficultés scolaires (ateliers d'éducation non formelle); 
2. Education à l’environnement (jardin partagé, jardin pédagogique, réemploi, recyclage…); 
3. Animation périscolaire (cantine le midi, projet éducatif en fin de journée…);
4. Promotion des dispositifs Européen pour la jeunesse (réseaux sociaux, témoignages, réunions d'information, etc.).
5. Participation à la vie de l'association et à ses temps forts annuels.

Hébergement : Les volontaires partageront un appartement, en chambres individuelles, situé dans la ville de Mulhouse, à 5mn de marche du lieu de mission. 
Restauration et argent de poche: les volontaires recevront une indemnité mensuelle pour couvrir leurs frais de nourriture et autres dépenses personnelles (argent de poche).

Jeunes femmes et jeunes hommes aimant le contact avec les enfants et les jeunes adultes. La/Le volontaire idéal fait preuve de flexibilité et de capacité d’adaptation, curieux, ouvert d’esprit et a le contact facile. Motivé pour prendre part à des projets collectifs au service du bien commun et de l’intérêt général dans un environnement multiculturel.

La mission se déroule dans une crèche de la ville de Dijon, très intéressée par les pratiques éducatives innovantes de la ville de Reggio Emilia, ville jumelle de Dijon, et de toute autre ville italienne. Les missions du ou de la jeune volontaire sont :
- Découvrir le modèle d'éducation de la petite enfance de Reggio Emilia et de ses environs et partager des idées pour l'aménagement des espaces intérieurs et extérieurs (photos, projets, etc.).
- Participer à la création d’"espaces aménagés extérieurs" et de jardins partagés avec les habitants du quartier
- Créer un lien avec un accueil Petite Enfance de Reggio Emilia et échanger de bonnes pratiques
- Documenter des idées de propositions pour faire émerger de nouvelles idées d'expression et de communication, en soulignant en particulier le rôle de l'art, de la nature et de l'ouverture sur le monde extérieur.

L'hébergement est assuré dans un appartement municipal, meublé et partagé avec d'autres volontaires. Il est situé à 10 minutes à pied du centre ville et du lieu de mission. Le jeune volontaire peut bénéficier du restaurant du personnel municipal à moindre coût, situé à côté de la crèche Tivoli. La ville est dotée d'un réseau de transports en commun (tram-bus), de pistes cyclables et de nombreuses zones piétonnes.
Un tarif réduit est proposé pour les moins de 26 ans (31 € par mois). Les informations sur le réseau sont facilement accessibles grâce à une application " Divia mobilités".

Le service mission Jeunesse accueille les jeunes volontaires à l'international et leur propose d'intégrer le parcours de cohésion dédiés aux jeunes volontaires. Au-delà des séminaires obligatoires, le parcours de cohésion permet de suivre une formation " Vie démocratique et organisation de la Ville de Dijon", une formation premiers secours et santé mentale et une découverte des services et métiers de la mairie,... D'autres formations peuvent être proposées par la Direction de la Petite Enfance.

- Intérêt pour la petite enfance et l'environnement; 
- Capacité à travailler en équipe ;
- Dynamisme et enthousiasme ;
-  Capacité à être créatif ; 
- Faire preuve de patience et de gentillesse avec les enfants ;
 - Avoir une connaissance de base du français.

Le/la volontaire participera à un large éventail d’activités au sein des différents pôles de l’association, en fonction de ses compétences et envies, notamment:

Animer des activités éducatives et créatives avec des enfants et des jeunes: 
Contribuer à l’aménagement du jardin communautaire et à la création d’un espace extérieur durable;
Participer à la rédaction du journal de l’association et à l’animation du blog, des réseaux sociaux et d’autres supports de communication;
Soutenir les équipes dans l’organisation de projets, d’évènements associatifs et de rencontre avec les partenaires;
Proposer des ateliers de langue pour différent publics, dans une approche non formelle;
Intervenir ponctuellement dans des écoles ou centres sociaux partenaires pour animer des ateliers auprès d’enfants, jeunes ou personnes âgées;
Participer à la promotion du Corps Européen de Solidarité et des programmes de mobilité;
Développer, s’il le souhaite, un projet personnel.

Le volontaire sera logé dans une maison partagée avec d’autres volontaires;
Déjeuner fourni chaque jour d’activité par l’association, une aide sera versée pour couvrir les reste des repas;
Argent de poche: 6€/jour;
Frais de transport local entre le logement et les activités pris en charge (abonnement mensuel);
Le transport est pris en charge par l’organisation d’accueil dans la limite d’un budget.

Être âgé de 18 à 30 ans
Être curieux, motivé, et ouvert à la rencontre interculturelle
Avoir envie de s’engager auprès des enfants, jeunes et personnes âgées
Être prêt à vivre et travailler dans un environnement rural
S’intéresser à l’éducation non formelle, l’écologie, la solidarité ou la communication
Être prêt à sortir de sa zone de confort et à vivre une expérience humaine, riche et collective.
